<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had sown 99.1 percent of wheat intentions of 6.789 million hectares by August 30, the Agriculture Secretariat it said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>Long-cycle wheat is developing well, as is wheat in Buenos Aires and La Pampa in general. But wheat in Cordoba, north-central Santa Fe, Entre Rios and northern La Pampa needs rain quickly to recuperate. About 9,300 hectares have been lost to drought in northern Entre Rios. Cotton harvesting finished, with raw output of 1.325 million tonnes, up 17.8 percemt from last season.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,789   99.1 (95.9)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,405  100.0(100.0)   2,610  100.0 (100.0)   (40.1)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,075  100.0(100.0)   5,990  100.0 (100.0)   (21.1)</p>
<p> Sunseed   3,389  100.0(100.0)   3,213  100.0 (100.0)   (17.0)</p>
<p> Sorghum     675  100.0(100.0)     557  100.0 (100.0)   (38.7)</p>
<p> Cotton    1,009  100.0  (n/a)     961   99.3 (100.0)   (13.7)</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541-318-0655</p>
